      "last_updated": "2026-08-29T00:00:00.000000",
      "description": "Which taxa change most in each contrast? One horizontal bar per taxon, showing its log fold change, for the 15 taxa with the largest absolute change in each contrast. Pink bars are more abundant in the contrast's group than in its reference group, blue bars less.\nHow to read: solid bars clear the significance cut-off and hatched bars do not, so only solid bars are calls. Long solid bars at either end are the taxa to check first. A panel of hatched bars means large changes without statistical support.\nLines and annotations: a line at zero separates higher from lower abundance. Solid against hatched applies the q-value cut-off of 0.05, the level ampliseq passes to ANCOM-BC, and no other cut-off line is drawn. Bar labels are the taxon names, cut at 24 characters (hover for the whole name).\nSources: ANCOM-BC, Lin and Peddada 2020, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-020-17041-7; ampliseq ANCOM-BC settings, https://github.com/nf-core/ampliseq/blob/2.18.0/conf/modules.config\nNote: only the 15 largest effects of each contrast are shown (Top-N), so a significant taxon with a modest change can be missing; the results table lists them all.",
      "title_size": "sm",
      "title_align": "left",
      "use": "qiime2/da_barplot",
      "catalog_source": {
        "toolId": "qiime2",
